  "observation": {
    "repeatability": "A second full run of this gate on the same server produced the same free trajectory, the same per-stop published counts and cycle counts, the same EOS-floor rows, and the same neighbour ids, so the measurement is reproducible rather than a single draw.",
    "cross_cell_identity": "The free trajectory and every stopped prefix were identical on INT8 and BF16. Cycle counts differed in one row (7 vs 8) while the published ids did not, so published output is the reproducible quantity across cells, not cycle timing.",
    "terminal_token": "Whether the stop token itself appears in generated_token_ids depends on where the stop lands relative to the chain: it is published when it is the chain's last visible token and withheld when the commit selects an earlier terminal prefix. Both arms agree in both cases, so this is the autoregressive convention, not a route difference."
